R('REQ-101','Status vocabulary, initial and finished words','PH-1',['ST-VOCAB','ST-FINISHED','DI-ARCHIVE'],
 'The words of a bound item are the `statuses` (and side words) of its definition; `initial` is the word of a new or newly bound item; a word in `finished` finishes the item for dependencies, archive and queue membership; `archived` must be a finished word and is written only by `backlog archive` (reserved storage word).',
 'Moves `src/shared/status.js` (which loads the shipped vocabulary into every command) into the definition.',
 ['A definition with other words works end to end (fixture `minimal.json`: ready → in progress → closed).','An unbound item is never compared with these words (REQ-902).'],
 [('a team with its own words',
   'Given a repository with a backlog\n  And the backlog registers the workflow "minimal" from the template "minimal.json"\n  And a team "t2" with lead "lead" and members "ann" using the workflow "minimal"\n  And I act as agent "lead"\n  And I run `backlog team new --team t2 --name "Mini" --objective o --summary s`\nThen item 1 has status "ready"\nWhen I act as agent "ann"\n  And I run `backlog team update 1 --team t2 --claim ann`\nThen item 1 has status "in progress"\nWhen I run `backlog team update 1 --team t2 --close --summary "done"`\nThen item 1 has status "closed"'),
  ('a finished word of the definition lets a dependent go',
   'Given a repository with a backlog\n  And the backlog registers the workflow "minimal" from the template "minimal.json" with `finished = ["closed","archived","dropped"] ; statuses = ["ready","in progress","dropped","closed","archived"]`\n  And a team "t2" with lead "lead" and members "ann" using the workflow "minimal"\n  And an item "A" exists\n  And item 1 has the front-matter fields `{"team":"t2","status":"dropped"}`\n  And an item "B" exists\n  And item 2 has the front-matter fields `{"team":"t2","status":"ready","depends_on":[1]}`\n  And I act as agent "ann"\n  And I have read item 2\nWhen I run `backlog team update 2 --team t2 --claim ann`\nThen the command succeeds')],
 [('engine-steps.test.js','statuses/initial/finished read from the definition','minimal.json','words used'),('engine-steps.test.js','archived reserved: only archive writes it','set-status to archived','refused'),('user-guard.test.js','src/shared/status.js removed','tree','absent')],F)
